    {
      "id": "G-_fmkM_dM2EvItOdq9ii",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 6528.087634948422,
      "y": -50.351147138659485,
      "width": 1855.835857611609,
      "height": 509.0315785030897,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "cross-hatch",
      "strokeWidth": 4,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 2,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [
        "53pSI3o6FXx6KVd-cPw_-"
      ],
      "frameId": null,
      "index": "b2JG",
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1557141964,
      "version": 634,
      "versionNonce": 586900882,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1769163089308,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "\"If we had forced flush() into the base LogHandler interface,\nConsoleHandler would have to either throw an exception or do\nnothing. That breaks LSP because you can't safely substitute\nConsoleHandler wherever LogHandler is expected.\nBy creating a separate FlushableHandler interface, each class\nonly implements what it actually needs. No exceptions, no empty\nmethods, no surprises.\"",
      "fontSize": 58.17503754321025,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "\"If we had forced flush() into the base LogHandler interface, ConsoleHandler would have to either throw an exception or do nothing. That breaks LSP because you can't safely substitute ConsoleHandler wherever LogHandler is expected.\nBy creating a separate FlushableHandler interface, each class only implements what it actually needs. No exceptions, no empty methods, no surprises.\"",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
